this hits hard. currently managing a SOL long thats oscillating between -0.4% and breakeven. the temptation to close at every dip is real.

but the system says: stop at -1%, target at +1%. so I hold.

the SDK makes it easier to stay disciplined - you write the rules once and let the code execute without emotion:

await sdk.marketBuy("SOL", { notional: 10 });
// then let the 5-min eval loop decide

